A||||7||William||Car sits 2 inches higher now||||5||
Z||000000||William||04-20-2001||01:45 PM||||After deciding to finish the front end rebuild, my car now sits 2 inches higher in the front. I replaced the balljoints, added KYB shocks and poly. Any idea here?||||reg||5
Z||000001||skitime||04-20-2001||02:10 PM||||Did you tighten the bushings while the suspension was hanging or did you preload the bushing by jacking under the lower A-arm to simulate weight?  Many people ruin new bushings by not preloading them before tightening them whether they are poly or rubber. If you didn't peload then the bushings will push the car up.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||ray b||04-20-2001||02:17 PM||||shocks too long ck part # or not compressing fully or sticky ,drive it some and see if it settles some. did you work the shocks before installing them?? or old ones were to low to start with. is front higher than back now or same?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||04-20-2001||02:46 PM||||Does the lower control arm hit the frame? When I did my suspension, If the lower control arm wasn't aligned prior (pre-loaded)<BR>It could be off and hitting the frame. Also Did you push down on the front or drive it? Mine had to settle also. After driving the suspension settled in and everything was fine.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Will||04-20-2001||03:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by skitime:<BR><B>Did you tighten the bushings while the suspension was hanging or did you preload the bushing by jacking under the lower A-arm to simulate weight?  Many people ruin new bushings by not preloading them before tightening them whether they are poly or rubber. If you didn't peload then the bushings will push the car up.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That only applies to rubber bushings because they work in torsional shear.<BR>Delrin or polyurethane slide across their inner sleeves. The problem with polyurethane is that it is a sticky plastic, not a slippery plastic, and it binds against its sleeves.||||reg||1
Z||000005||William||04-20-2001||06:44 PM||||I will drive it and see if it settles. The front is way higher than the back. It looks like it's parked on a hill. Boy' is it tight. Very little deflection when pushing down. Maybe I didn't ream the bushings too much after all.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero56||04-20-2001||08:10 PM||||William, everytime I raise the front end of my Formula(with poly bushings)it sits several inches higher than normal height. It always go to proper height after driving it.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Seanh||04-20-2001||09:05 PM||||I would be almost tempted to say they could be the wrong shocks. I bought some at Advanced auto and they gave me the ones their computer said were right, but they were way to big, it was obvious when comparing it to the old shock. I took em back and NAPA got me the correct ones. ||||reg||1
